sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as User
    participant G as Tk GUI thread
    participant AQ as UI queue
    participant AW as Action worker thread(s)
    participant RW as Refresh worker thread(s)
    participant PM as PiStreamerManager
    participant SSH as ssh subprocess
    participant PI as Pi process state

    U->>G: Click Start Mic
    G->>G: status_label="Starting..."
    G->>AW: spawn _streamer_action_worker(mic,start)
    AW->>PM: run_action(mic,start)
    PM->>SSH: subprocess.run(..., timeout=20)

    U->>G: Click Start Video (before first completes)
    G->>G: status_label="Starting..."
    G->>AW: spawn _streamer_action_worker(video,start)
    AW->>PM: run_action(video,start) (waits on PM lock)

    note over SSH,PI: Intermittent long SSH session; remote side may still launch streamer
    PI-->>PI: streamer becomes alive
    SSH-->>PM: TimeoutExpired => None
    PM-->>AW: (False, "ssh-failed")
    AW->>AQ: post status_label="ssh-failed" (no refresh on failure)

    PM->>SSH: queued next start now executes; may also timeout
    SSH-->>PM: TimeoutExpired => None
    PM-->>AW: (False, "ssh-failed")
    AW->>AQ: post status_label="ssh-failed"

    par Other trigger (startup/manual/success path)
        G->>RW: refresh_streamer_status(...)
        RW->>PM: query_status(...)
        PM->>SSH: subprocess.run(..., timeout=12)
        SSH-->>PM: "running"
        PM-->>RW: (True, "running")
        RW->>AQ: post status_label="running"
    and UI drain
        G->>AQ: periodic drain every 20ms
        AQ-->>G: apply queued callbacks FIFO
    end

    note over G: Final visible label depends on callback arrival order,\nnot on operation recency/intent.
